# probe-04 optional_budget_cliff
# GAP: the LIMIT row-budget forwards through only offset/join/limit/graph/dataset/project/
#   union/bind (F17 added UNION+BIND). OptionalOperator has NO set_row_budget impl, so it
#   inherits the no-op default and SWALLOWS the budget: a LIMIT above an OPTIONAL does not
#   bound the driving FACT scan.
# MECHANISM that SHOULD fire: LIMIT budget forwarding into the required (left) child scan.
# CONTRAST: probe-04b (same, no OPTIONAL) DOES budget-cap the scan to ~50 rows.
# PREDICTED: full FACT_ORDER materialize (window not capped to 50), wall >> the plain
#   LIMIT-50 form; scan_table present with large emitted-row count before the LIMIT clips.
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?oid ?tot ?cust
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:orderId ?oid ; edw:orderTotal ?tot .
        OPTIONAL { ?o edw:customer ?cust . } }
LIMIT 50
